2026-10-31T00:00:02Z (RFD66606-2369) 'The standalone headset draws at most 700k triangles in view per frame, split between world and characters.
 # tags: rfd:hook
 Text:RFD2369  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:03Z (RFD66606-2369) 'Past 700k triangles in view the frame is over the operator's budget, and the crowd of non-player characters is the first to drop to impostors.
 # tags: rfd:intrigue
 Text:RFD2369  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:04Z (RFD66606-2369) 'Check a scene against the budget: at most 700k triangles in view per frame, 250k for world geometry and 450k for characters.
 # tags: rfd:exit
 Text:RFD2369  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:05Z (RFD66606-2369) 'the standalone headset draws at most 700k triangles
 # tags: rfd:details-title, rfd:no-final-newline
 Text:RFD2369  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:06Z (RFD66606-2369) 'The operator's budget for the standalone headset: at most 700k triangles in view per frame, of which world geometry gets 250k (400k at most) and characters 450k. A crowd of non-player characters holds 150k of the character share and drops to impostors first. One equal-error LOD threshold over the frame enforces it, and the LODs come from Godot's own `generate_lods` on welded meshes, except the blossom cards, whose levels are the cluster LOD DAGs of RFD66606-2367.
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2369  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:07Z (RFD66606-2369) '- RFD66606-2294, where this rule lived before the split.
